I built and saved the workflow, but I couldn't confirm it starts a call. The one live chat test came back with a 504 (gateway timeout) on the second try, and the first try got no answer within 60 seconds. A 504 isn't the 500 that would mean the workflow is broken, so it may just be the platform being slow, but nothing has run end to end yet. The rule-by-rule re-read of the brief against the workflow (step 7) also didn't happen because time ran out.

- **Checks:** the lint step and `situations.py check` both passed with no problems.
- **How it runs:** the call starts in the date-facts code node, then opening, then identity. After identity, `get_account` runs (with the account hook from the calc file) and goes to a router that states every late product. From there it goes to `negotiate` or one of the six specialist nodes: `refused`, `hardship`, `dispute`, `already_paid`, `restructuring` and `human`. Each node closes the call through `close_call` and then hangs up.
- **Rules no code computes:** I wrote both into the node that applies them. The date-of-birth format rule is in identity, and the "one date for everything" rule is in negotiate.
- **Brief vs. extracted situations:** I found no differences, so I didn't override any of them.
- **Files:** the workflow is `out/w4-B-c1.workflow.json`, built by `out/w4-B-c1.gen.py`.

