Both errors are fixed: buildcheck now prints `ok` with no ERROR, and the JSON loads.

**Cause:** `{{title}}` and `{{last_name}}` are real call variables. Brief A section 2 lists `customer_id`, `first_name`, `last_name`, `title` and `now`, and the opening line in the brief says "Am I speaking with {title} {last_name}?". But the workflow never declared them anywhere the checker could see. The checker treats the top-level `test_variables` block (the default values for call variables) as the list of declared call variables, and this workflow had no such block.

**Fix:** with Edit, I added one top-level line to `out/w4-B-c1.workflow.json`, with the example values from the brief:
```json
"test_variables": {"customer_id": "c_test", "first_name": "Daniel", "last_name": "Reyes", "title": "Mr", "now": "2026-10-14T11:00"}
```
I left the prompts as they are, because asking for the customer by title and last name is what the brief requires.

Nothing else changed: no prompts, nodes, transitions, the start code node or any pre/post-process code. Nothing was saved to Freya.

The values in that block are test defaults. They are only used when a call doesn't pass its own `title` and `last_name`, so a real call still uses the actual customer's details.

